## Milestone 1 — Schema Hardening
**Goal:** Make the DB schema fully reflect the business rules (state machine, TTL support)
**Estimated effort:** ~1 hour

### Tasks

#### 1.1 — Add `PROCESSING` to `PaymentStatus` enum
```prisma
// schema.prisma
enum PaymentStatus {
  PENDING
  PROCESSING   ← ADD THIS
  SUCCESS
  FAILED
  CANCELLED
  TIMED_OUT    ← ADD THIS
  REFUNDED
  PARTIALLY_REFUNDED
}
```
**Why:** Rule 8 requires `PENDING → PROCESSING → SUCCESS/FAILED`.
Right now the controller jumps from `PENDING` directly to `SUCCESS`, which skips `PROCESSING`. The webhook handler does update to `PROCESSING` via `WebhookEvent` but the `Payment` row itself never enters a `PROCESSING` state. This must be explicit.

#### 1.2 — Add `expiresAt` to `Payment` model
```prisma
model Payment {
  ...
  expiresAt  DateTime?   ← ADD THIS (Rule 11 — TTL)
}
```
**Why:** The expiry job (Milestone 3) needs to know when to time out a stale attempt.

#### 1.3 — Run migration
```bash
npx prisma migrate dev --name add_payment_processing_states
```

#### 1.4 — Update `paymentSummary.js`
- Add `PROCESSING` and `TIMED_OUT` to the status handling logic in `getPaymentSummary()`.
- Add new `paymentState` values: `"PROCESSING"`, `"TIMED_OUT"`.

### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Migration runs without errors.
- [ ] `PROCESSING` and `TIMED_OUT` are valid values in Prisma client.
- [ ] `getPaymentSummary()` handles the new states without crashing.
- [ ] Existing 29 unit tests still pass.

