## Milestone 2 — Controller Hardening
**Goal:** Apply missing business rules directly to the controller logic
**Estimated effort:** ~2–3 hours

### Tasks

#### 2.1 — Add `PROCESSING` transition in `createPaymentOrder`
When a new `Payment` record is created and a Razorpay Order is successfully obtained, immediately transition `Payment` status from `PENDING → PROCESSING` before returning to the frontend.

```
Create Payment (PENDING)
    → createRazorpayOrder()
    → Save gatewayOrderId
    → Update Payment status = PROCESSING   ← NEW STEP
    → Return to frontend
```

**Why:** Rule 8 — while the customer is inside Razorpay Checkout, the attempt should be `PROCESSING`, not `PENDING`. This clearly signals "a live checkout is happening right now."

#### 2.2 — Set `expiresAt` when creating a payment attempt
When creating a new `Payment` record, set:
```js
expiresAt: new Date(now().getTime() + 15 * 60 * 1000) // 15 minutes
```
**Why:** Rule 11 — the expiry job (Milestone 3) needs this field.

#### 2.3 — Guard `createPaymentOrder` against `PROCESSING` status
Update the active attempt detection logic to also treat `PROCESSING` as an active/blocking attempt:
```js
// Current check
item.status === "PENDING"
// New check
["PENDING", "PROCESSING"].includes(item.status)
```
**Why:** Rule 4 — overlapping attempts must be blocked even if the first is in `PROCESSING`.

#### 2.4 — Validate `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` on app startup
In `app.js` or `server.js`, add a startup check:
```js
if (!process.env.RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  console.warn("⚠️  RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET is not set. Webhooks will be rejected.");
}
```
**Why:** Fail-fast principle — surface misconfiguration early instead of silently failing at runtime.

#### 2.5 — Update existing unit tests for new state transitions
- Update tests that assert `status === "PENDING"` mid-flow to assert `status === "PROCESSING"`.
- Add new test: `"payment transitions to PROCESSING after Razorpay order is created"`.
- Add new test: `"PROCESSING attempt blocks a new attempt (Rule 4)"`.
- Add new test: `"expiresAt is set on new payment attempt"`.

### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] New payments transition `PENDING → PROCESSING` after Razorpay order creation.
- [ ] `expiresAt` is populated on every new `Payment` record.
- [ ] `PROCESSING` attempts block new checkout initiations.
- [ ] All unit tests pass (including new ones).

